  "title": "The Monday Meeting Mix-up",
  "category": "work-admin",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "level": 7,
  "order": 706,
  "theme": "work",
  "culturalNote": "Kenyan offices run on WhatsApp groups, tea breaks, and meetings that move. Passive verbs are how office news travels: \"mkutano umeahirishwa\" (the meeting has been postponed), \"ripoti iliandikwa na Faith\" (the report was written by Faith), \"tuliambiwa\" (we were told). Reciprocals describe teamwork: tunasaidiana (we help each other), tujadiliane (let's discuss it together).",
  "startingPoint": "You arrive at the conference room at 9 a.m. for the weekly meeting. It's empty. Wanjiku walks past.",
  "grammarFocus": [
